{
  "summary": "This PR refactors multiple internal functions across chain management, block index handling, block filters, and peer processing to accept `CBlockIndex` by reference instead of pointer where null arguments are prohibited. It also switches `CChain`'s internal storage vector from raw `CBlockIndex*` pointers to `std::reference_wrapper<CBlockIndex>` and renames several `FindNextBlocks` parameters to snake_case.",
  "problem": "Functions that take raw pointers even when null is prohibited fail to enforce or document non-null invariants through the type system, increasing the risk of nullptr dereference errors in future modifications and prompting redundant caller checks.",
  "evidence": [
    "Author notes the motivation is a \"slight improvement in code quality, maintainability and robustness\" by creating a \"more explicit representation of the non-null input invariant\" as a continuation of merged PR #34440."
  ],
  "dependencies": {
    "depends_on": [],
    "enables": []
  },
  "scope_notes": "Includes cosmetic parameter renames to snake_case in `PeerManagerImpl::FindNextBlocks` alongside the signature refactors.",
  "changed_since_previous": "Added a commit that renames the parameters of `PeerManagerImpl::FindNextBlocks` to snake_case (such as `vBlocks` to `blocks` and `pindexWalk` to `index_walk`).",
  "card": "This pull request converts `CBlockIndex` pointer parameters to references across `LastCommonAncestor`, block filter range lookups, `BaseIndex::ProcessBlock`, and `PeerManagerImpl` block download helpers where null is invalid. It also changes `CChain`'s internal storage vector to use `std::reference_wrapper<CBlockIndex>` instead of raw pointers and updates several function parameter names to snake_case. The change addresses internal type safety and non-null invariant enforcement in chain and P2P code paths. The author frames this purely as a janitorial code-quality refactor continuing from merged PR #34440.",
